{"title":"2013 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/259d1d91a5687fe90489d9efeeab80c4de05cf5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQRS$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"54\" height=\"16\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/f/acf35ddb2ff553da32a2eef0837f4f4bfa0bf43b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"18\" /> and rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" /> has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/0/26006b598ef38acb074305f8eda697e74c71dc1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ZY = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/434b43c3ed50dfcfe55a5a68619bfe75826a1aee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WX$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/9/f0937ede81ec8f60015799b03b6bd7007330cf55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SR$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/0/470be42e6d69799e4acd5f771a7e3238bb300d9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SX = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/6/336fbb3fa827af62a349b31cc5e18558d299f358.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> equals\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/f/d6ff262c8bfefcf9b72454ded826f3f9b4c63b53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 20 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 25 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 55 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 45 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/a/88a264852ec158457543f490d3ddd93d1a69983a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WX = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" /> because it is parallel to side length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/a/3aab17e2f2005ca643854186430099294ad84b85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZ$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> in rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/0/2b076f2e7f124fc5d8b5ef7b30b95bfcfe85449f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WXYZ$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />, which has a side length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. This means that they are equal to each other. Using similar logic with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/9/f0937ede81ec8f60015799b03b6bd7007330cf55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SR$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac4c03816d8db6099dcf2ac4a734b7ef6461f51e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SR = PQ = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>We can add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/434b43c3ed50dfcfe55a5a68619bfe75826a1aee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WX$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/9/f0937ede81ec8f60015799b03b6bd7007330cf55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SR$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> together to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/6/336fbb3fa827af62a349b31cc5e18558d299f358.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WR$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />. However, we notice from the diagram that we count the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd7db9202db08b7c54a81c8afecf617b8a479fd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> twice in the computation when we do that because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/4/434b43c3ed50dfcfe55a5a68619bfe75826a1aee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WX$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/9/f0937ede81ec8f60015799b03b6bd7007330cf55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SR$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> overlap with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/7/dd7db9202db08b7c54a81c8afecf617b8a479fd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/c/89caf5e7a718a07bf5dfa170ee0df22a3a3d4d13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WR = WX + SR - SX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"195\" height=\"16\" />. Plugging in the values we have, this gives:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/9/219a5846ec358ae99aeb4680cc1b056ba9447054.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$WR = 15 + 30 - 10 = 45 - 10 = \\boxed {\\textbf {(E) } 35}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"329\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"2013 CEMC Fermat\">2013 CEMC Fermat</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Fermat Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Fermat Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2013 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2013 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 6 (page does not exist)\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3